# Screen toys: animations and effects, one stanza per program.  The
# play-tests in tools/playtests cover bite, card, life, rain, suicide and
# worms.

shot    suicide1
cap     A rooftop animation drawn in characters: a stick figure jumps
cap     from the top of a tower block and a long scream runs along the
cap     roofline as it falls.  It plays once, a few seconds, and returns
cap     to the prompt.  It draws with the terminal's termcap entry.
try     suicide1
run     suicide1
wait    6
snap
wait    2

shot    suicide2
cap     The same rooftop animation with a different ending: a car comes
cap     along the road at the foot of the building, and somebody shouts
cap     a warning across the top of the screen.  It plays once and
cap     returns to the prompt.
try     suicide2
run     suicide2
wait    6
snap
wait    2

shot    ttyexp
size    30 80
cap     Fireworks for a terminal: bursts of characters are thrown out
cap     from a point, arc under gravity and fall away, with trails.  Each
cap     option is one letter and a number: -s how many bursts at once,
cap     -p how many points in each, -x and -y the size, -w a wind, -D how
cap     many seconds it runs.  It clears the screen when it is done.
try     ttyexp -s2 -p50
run     ttyexp -s2 -p50
wait    3
snap
wait    2
snap
wait    7

shot    xmas
size    24 80
cap     A Christmas card drawn in characters: the tree is drawn and trimmed,
cap     lights blink along its strings, and reindeer run across the screen
cap     before the card starts over.  It loops until control-C.
try     xmas
run     xmas
wait    60
snap
send    \003
wait    2
